# Problem  Statement 
The purpose of this project is to develop a simple tic-tac-toe game using python. The game allows two players to play on a 3*3 boaed.The program takes player input, validates the move, updates the board, and checks whether a player has won or the game has ended in a draw.
## Scope of the project 
The project focuses on developing a basic two- player tic tac toe game using python. It includes a game board,player input,input validation, winner checking, draw detection, and an option to play again.
The project is mainely designed to demonstrate basic python programming concepts such as functions, lists,loops, conditional statements, and error handling.
## Target Users
The target users of this project are:
Students learning python programming.
Beginners who want to understand basic game development.
Users who want to play a simple two-player tic tac toe game
## High-level features
3*3 tic tac toe game board.
Two-player gameplay using X and O.
Player input from positions 1 to 9.
Validation of player moves.
Detection of winning combinations.
Detection of draw condition.
Option to play the game again.
Error handling for invalid input.
## Project Type
Individual python project
## Programming Language
python
